course: dictionary
lesson: 1957
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around them, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «LEGO is a Danish company founded in 1932.» Here a company is a business that makes things and sells them.
explain: Now read this: «Grandma came to stay, so we had company all week.» The clue is "came to stay", so company must mean visitors, people in your home. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Company can also mean being with someone so they are not alone. «Every pet has five needs: ... company, or the right to live alone if that suits it.» Here company means togetherness. Read the whole sentence: the clues tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Company is a noun, and it has several meanings. Use the context to choose the right one.
fact: «Company» can mean a business that makes or sells things, or provides a service.
fact: «Company» can mean being with other people, so you are not alone. «Keep someone company» means stay with them.
fact: «Company» can mean guests or visitors in your home.
fact: «Company» can mean a group of actors, dancers or soldiers who work together, as in «a theatre company».
exercise: «LEGO is a Danish company founded in 1932.» What does company mean here? | Being with someone so they are not alone | Visitors who stay in your home | *A business that makes and sells things
exercise: «We have company tonight, so please tidy your room.» What does company mean here? | A business that sells toys | A group of actors who work together | *Visitors coming to your home
exercise: «Our cat keeps me company when I read.» What does company mean here? | Guests who stay for a week | A company that makes cat food | *Being with someone so you are not alone
test: «The theatre company practised for months before the show.» What does company mean here? | A business that sells tickets | Visitors in the audience | *A group of actors who work together
test: Pets are good company, so a lonely child might ask for one. Which phrase means stay with someone so they are not lonely? | *Keep someone company | Part company | A toy company
exam: «Real game companies never ask for your password on another website or in chat.» What does company mean here? | *A business that makes and sells games | A group of players who work together | Guests visiting a house | Being with friends online
